00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:29.000
Lecturer: Let's start with actors. An actor is a role that interacts with the system from outside.

38
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:59.000
Lecturer: A role, not a person. The same person can be a Member in the morning and a Librarian in the afternoon.

39
00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:29.000
Lecturer: Actors can also be other systems, like the payment provider or the university's student records.

40
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:59.000
Lecturer: The primary actor is the one whose goal the use case serves. Supporting actors help along the way.

41
00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:29.000
Lecturer: A good test: is it outside the system boundary, and does it want something from the system?

42
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:59.000
Lecturer: The database is not an actor. It's part of your system. This is the mistake I see most.

