00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Lecturer: Now goals. Every use case is named after the goal of its primary actor, as a verb phrase.

72
00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:59.000
Lecturer: Borrow a book. Reserve a title. Pay a fine. Not 'Book management' and not 'Login'.

73
00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:29.000
Lecturer: Logging in is rarely a goal on its own. Nobody wakes up wanting to log in.

74
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:59.000
Lecturer: Ask: if the actor did only this and went home, would they be satisfied? That's the right level.

75
00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:29.000
Lecturer: Too high, like 'Run the library', and you can't write steps. Too low, like 'Click OK', and you drown in detail.

