00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:29.000
Lecturer: The heart of a use case is the main flow, also called the main success scenario.

106
00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:59.000
Lecturer: Write it as numbered steps, each one an actor doing something or the system responding.

107
00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:29.000
Lecturer: Keep each step at one level: 'The member scans their card', not 'the member moves their hand'.

108
00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:59.000
Lecturer: No user interface details. Don't write 'clicks the blue button'; write 'confirms the loan'.

109
00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:29.000
Lecturer: Three to nine steps is usually right. If you have twenty, you probably have two use cases.

110
00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:59.000
Lecturer: The main flow assumes everything goes well. What goes wrong comes next.

